---
stories: prop[list]
---
<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Newsroom</h1>
<p class="mt-3 text-foreground-second">An API with three levels of access, each a guard on a controller or a method. Under <code>nx dev</code>, <code>/docs</code> lists every route.</p>

<div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto">
<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
  <caption class="sr-only">Who may call which route</caption>
  <thead><tr class="border-b border-border"><th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Route</th><th scope="col" class="py-2 font-semibold">Who</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr class="border-b border-border"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>GET /api/stories/</code>, <code>GET /api/stories/{slug}/</code></td><td class="py-2">anyone</td></tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-border"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>GET</code>, <code>POST /api/drafts/</code></td><td class="py-2">a key</td></tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-border"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>POST /api/drafts/{slug}/publish/</code>, <code>DELETE /api/stories/{slug}/</code></td><td class="py-2">an editor's key</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Published</h2>
<ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5">
  {% for story in stories %}<li><a href="/api/stories/{{ story.slug }}/" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center">{{ story.title | e }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
